From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:15:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] DVDDemuxFFmpeg: fix .sup seeks to before the first packet

A .sup seek target gets no start time offset, so a seek back to the
start or to an early chapter can lie before the first packet. The
backward seek then fails, the file keeps its old position, and the
subtitles in between are not shown.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -0,6 +0,10 @@
       ret = av_seek_frame(m_pFormatContext, m_seekStream, seek_pts,
                           backwards ? AVSEEK_FLAG_BACKWARD : 0);
 
+    // a .sup target can lie before the first packet, where a backward seek fails
+    if (ret < 0 && m_bSup && seek_pts < m_pFormatContext->start_time)
+      ret = av_seek_frame(m_pFormatContext, m_seekStream, seek_pts, 0);
+
     if (ret < 0)
     {
       // demuxer can return failure, if seeking behind eof
